{"path":"thread/unique_lock/lock","title":"std::unique_lock<Mutex>::lock","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::unique_lock&lt;Mutex&gt;::</span>lock","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/unique_lock/lock","section":"thread","kind":"page","summary":"Locks (i.e., takes ownership of) the associated mutex. Effectively calls mutex()->lock().","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> lock<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Locks (i.e., takes ownership of) the associated mutex. Effectively calls <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">mutex<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>lock<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<ul><li> Any exceptions thrown by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">mutex<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>lock<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</li></ul>\n<ul><li> If there is no associated mutex, <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/system_error\">std::system_error</a></span> with an error code of <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/errc\">std::errc::operation_not_permitted</a></span>.\n</li></ul>\n<ul><li> If the mutex is already locked by this <code>unique_lock</code> (in other words, <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/unique_lock/owns_lock\">owns_lock()</a></span> is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>), <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/system_error\">std::system_error</a></span> with an error code of <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/errc\">std::errc::resource_deadlock_would_occur</a></span>.\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\"><p>The following example uses <code>lock</code> to re-acquire a mutex that was unlocked.</p>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;chrono&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;mutex&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;thread&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;vector&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> counter <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/mutex\"><span class=\"kw2175\">std::<span class=\"me2\">mutex</span></span></a> counter_mutex<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector\"><span class=\"kw1277\">std::<span class=\"me2\">vector</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/thread\"><span class=\"kw2167\">std::<span class=\"me2\">thread</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> threads<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> worker_task <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span> id<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/unique_lock\"><span class=\"kw2188\">std::<span class=\"me2\">unique_lock</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/mutex\"><span class=\"kw2175\">std::<span class=\"me2\">mutex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> lock<span class=\"br0\">(</span>counter_mutex<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>counter<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> id <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\", initial counter: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> counter <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        lock.<span class=\"me1\">unlock</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n        <span class=\"co1\">// don't hold the lock while we simulate an expensive operation</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/sleep_for\"><span class=\"kw2170\">std::<span class=\"me2\">this_thread</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">sleep_for</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/duration\"><span class=\"kw1001\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">seconds</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n        lock.<span class=\"me1\">lock</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>counter<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> id <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\", final counter: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> counter <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span> i <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> i <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"nu0\">10</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>i<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        threads.<span class=\"me1\">emplace_back</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>worker_task, i<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">auto</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> thread <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> threads<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        thread.<span class=\"me1\">join</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>0, initial counter: 1\n1, initial counter: 2\n2, initial counter: 3\n3, initial counter: 4\n4, initial counter: 5\n5, initial counter: 6\n6, initial counter: 7\n7, initial counter: 8\n8, initial counter: 9\n9, initial counter: 10\n6, final counter: 11\n3, final counter: 12\n4, final counter: 13\n2, final counter: 14\n5, final counter: 15\n0, final counter: 16\n1, final counter: 17\n7, final counter: 18\n9, final counter: 19\n8, final counter: 20</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/unique_lock/try_lock\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>try_lock</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  tries to lock (i.e., takes ownership of) the associated mutex without blocking <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/unique_lock/unlock\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>unlock</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  unlocks (i.e., releases ownership of) the associated mutex <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"thread","title":"Concurrency support library (since C++11)"},{"path":"thread/unique_lock","title":"std::unique_lock"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::unique_lock<Mutex>::lock","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++11. Locks (i.e., takes ownership of) the associated mutex. Effectively calls mutex()->lock()."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Exceptions"},{"label":"Example","note":"The following example uses lock to re-acquire a mutex that was unlocked."},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"try_lock","note":"tries to lock (i.e., takes ownership of) the associated mutex without blocking"},{"label":"unlock","note":"unlocks (i.e., releases ownership of) the associated mutex"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":274,"codeBlockCount":2}
